{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_5cag22wcmvxnuddoksflemns5ybnwpiopt2x5ap2mjdntrqs5a6a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 3 tests pass. The build succeeds and `cargo test` runs successfully:\n\n- `test_parser_hello_world` ✓\n- `test_parser_gamut` ✓\n- `test_program_execution_count` ✓\n\nSummary of the implementation:\n\n1. **`src/throw.rs`** — Replaced `mathErr`/`opErr` with Rust equivalents that print to stderr and abort (matching the C `raise(SIGFPE)`/`raise(SIGILL)` semantics).\n\n2. **`src/stack.rs`** — Implemented a singly-linked list stack using safe Rust (`Box<ListNode>`/`Option`). Implemented an iterative `Drop` to avoid stack overflow on long stacks.\n\n3. **`src/parser.rs`** — Implemented `parse`, `readline`, `prog_len`, and `free_program`. Faithfully reproduces the C parser's keyword scanning logic (`slothy`, `sloth`, `and`, `nap`) plus the `had_token` line-handling.\n\n4. **`src/slothvm.rs`** — Implemented `execute` matching every opcode in the C VM (EXIT, PUSH, ADD, SUB, MULT, DIV, COMP with all comparison codes, INP/OUT for INT/CHR types, GOTO, DUP), including division-by-zero / overflow checks.\n\n5. **`src/sloth.rs`** — Implemented `main` to mirror `c_src/sloth.c`'s CLI behavior (parse file from argv[1], execute, print result).\n\nNo `unsafe`, no FFI, no remaining `unimplemented!()`/`todo!()`/`panic!()` placeholders."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1132,"cache_read_input_tokens":41224,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1132,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f72a7e15-a137-4ee4-8935-a5ce971d16db","uuid":"8b9f97cf-1c4d-4966-9eaa-7a5755e96fbc"}
